# Authority

Follow root `CLAUDE.md` and `process/README.md`. Bricks on this site is **1.12.3**.

`reference/Brick-Build-Page` is Bricks **2.3.6** (PLAN/DO/DONE, hand-written JSON, `bricks-mcp`, `get_design_context`). Do not use those skills, rules, or scripts for a build, a template, or an edit under `process/` or `wp-content/` in this repo.

A page follows `.claude/commands/generate-page-from-figma.md` and `node process/auto.mjs`. One template follows `.claude/commands/generate-template-from-figma.md` and `node process/template.mjs`. Those two commands are the only workflows. Read the matching command before building.

While a workflow runs: reply in Vietnamese, short, do the step, then stop. Ask for a missing breakpoint link. Do not guess a URL, alt, or FAQ answer.

Eight engine steps stay in code: fetch, tree, detect, export, build, push, verify, summary. A template `read` stops after detect and writes `plan.md` in the frame folder. The chat only points to that file. Build starts after the owner sets `Xác nhận: có`.

The picture and the tree decide what a group is. A repeated child shape counts (the Figma hover: selected layer = highlighted box). A layer name matching `tab` / `menu` / `nav` / `button` is a hint, not a gate. Layer names in these files are inconsistent. Do not add a name regex for one file.

No whack-a-mole. A miss is a gap in the shared rule, not a patch for that file. Before changing detect or render, read the catalog, `process/modules/recognize-parts/structure.mjs`, and one other section with the same shape. The change has to serve the next Figma file and still pass the existing tests. Recognize from two inputs together: the tree, and a picture (Figma's own frame render, or the Playwright shot from Docker verify). The picture says what the group is. The tree supplies the numbers. Do not measure pixels off a screenshot. The owner reviews the plan once, so do that work before showing it, then wait.

# Never

- No git writes: commit, add, push, branch, tag, stash, reset, checkout, PR. Read-only git is fine. Say when a change is ready and stop.
- Do not hand-write or patch `bricks.json`. A wrong look is fixed in `process/modules/write-bricks/render/`, `process/modules/approve-parts/`, `policy.json`, or `overrides.json`, with a test.
- Do not invent pixels, URLs, alt text, tooltip copy, or FAQ answers. Report the Figma value and what Bricks does. Do not loosen a check to make it pass.
- Do not open a browser or GUI on this machine. Verify with Playwright in Docker (`process/modules/common/qa.mjs`).
- Do not print `.env`.
